From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 13:41:44 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: dispcc-glymur: Make the DPTX0 DP-IN link divider
 writable

The DPTX0 DP-IN link divider feeds the link clock of DisplayPort
controller 0 to the USB4 router's DP IN adapter. That adapter takes
wider symbols at HBR2 and HBR3, so the divider has to be set to 1, 2 or
4 depending on the link rate while the link clock itself stays at the
PHY rate.

The divider is described with read-only ops and CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT, so
a rate request on it changes the shared DPTX0 link clock source instead.
Use the writable divider ops and stop forwarding rate requests to the
parent.

Assisted-by: Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/clk/qcom/dispcc-glymur.c | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/dispcc-glymur.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/dispcc-glymur.c
index 32cc5226b4d..2a9c4ae37d4 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/dispcc-glymur.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/dispcc-glymur.c
@@ -787,8 +787,7 @@ static struct clk_regmap_div disp_cc_mdss_dptx0_link_dpin_div_clk_src = {
 			&disp_cc_mdss_dptx0_link_clk_src.clkr.hw,
 		},
 		.num_parents = 1,
-		.flags = CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT,
-		.ops = &clk_regmap_div_ro_ops,
+		.ops = &clk_regmap_div_ops,
 	},
 };
 
